# Postgres. No secret in this repo has a real value: the repo is public.
#
# Supabase, provisioned through Vercel's integration, exposes two connection strings that are
# not interchangeable. The app needs the pooled one; migrations and ingest need the direct one.
# See db/env.ts. Neither has a default: the app and the scripts both refuse to start without
# one.
#
# The app (db/client.ts) reads the first of these that is set:
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
# POSTGRES_URL is Vercel's Supabase integration's own name for the pooled (PgBouncer,
# transaction-mode) connection string, read when DATABASE_URL is not set.
# POSTGRES_URL=

# Migrations (drizzle.config.ts) and ingest (db/migration-client.ts) read the first of these
# that is set. POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING is Vercel's Supabase integration's name for the direct,
# non-pooling connection string that DDL and prepared statements need; DATABASE_URL and
# POSTGRES_URL above are the fallbacks.
# POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING=
